# {{ .Name }}

A Civitai App Block (Vite + React, config-as-code build).

## What this is

A sandboxed static web app served in an iframe by the Civitai host. The
platform owns the build: it runs `npm ci` and then the `buildCommand` from
`block.manifest.json` (`npm run build`), serving the static output from
`outputDir` (`dist/`). You do NOT commit `dist/` — the platform builds it.

## Develop

```bash
npm install
npm run dev      # http://localhost:5173
```

Build locally to sanity-check what the platform will produce:

```bash
npm run build && npm run preview
```

## Validate

```bash
civitai app validate
```

## Submit

```bash
civitai login        # once, to store your API token
civitai app submit
```

`submit` packages the SOURCE tree (manifest + src + build config), excluding
`.git`, `node_modules`, and `dist` — the platform rebuilds from source.
